 established in 1931-03-19. A moderately significant entity in the historical record. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "The Republican Left of Catalonia (Esquerra Republicana de Catalunya, ERC) emerged on March 19, 1931, in Barcelona, as a pivotal political party advocating for Catalan independence and socialism. Founded during a time of significant socio-political upheaval in Spain, it represented a crucial faction in the broader struggle for regional autonomy and leftist ideals. Its establishment coincided with the proclamation of the Second Spanish Republic, marking a significant shift in the political landscape of Spain and the Catalan territories.

